                <pb facs="1050" n="948" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg948"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.01 Foreign Control/952: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hibbard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-06-08T11:00:00-00:44">June 8, 1935—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:32 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>18. My telegram No. 17, June 6, 3 p.m. The bills covering Firestone agreements
                    and repeal legislation were signed by the President yesterday afternoon. Copies
                    will be sent by pouch June 18.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hibbard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
